Z||000000||Jncomutt||12-13-2001||04:58 PM||||Was lookin at the pics of AusFieros door pods and they're great.  I'm havin trouble finding the 6" speakers but my other question is, can they be used without power windows.<P>It looks as though the crank may get in the way but just want to make sure first.||||reg||1
Z||000001||AusFiero||12-13-2001||06:08 PM||||hmmm good point. Does the existing door pocket get in the way of the crank? If not all will be fine as the doop pods do not go any higher up than them. <P>------------------<BR>         <IMG SRC="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero/auschristmas.gif">        <BR><A HREF="http://www.jadeweb.com.au/fiero" TARGET=_blank>My Fiero</A> | <A HREF="http://www.fieroshop.com.au" TARGET=_blank>Fiero Accessories</A>||202.139.20.3||reg||1
Z||000002||Pyric||12-13-2001||06:54 PM||||Does anyone have some pictures of those installed?  I've seen them by themselves on the site, but not actually on the door.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Phil||12-13-2001||06:54 PM||||On a manual window the crank comes right through the middle of where the map pocket "would" be located. Manual window cars don't have pockets.||||reg||1
Z||000004||AusFiero||12-13-2001||07:07 PM||||Not a real good angle but you can just see them.<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/interior01_7.jpg"> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroBUZZ||12-13-2001||07:17 PM||||I figure there are several alternatives. You can get a 4" round or a 4x6 in a pod between the crank and the door pull. Or you can make an extension for the crank and fit in a slightly larger speaker. Yes, the crank will stick in your leg (unless you make it removeable). Pods need to be remade for we crankers, in the end I decided to get electric windows.<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signat.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by FieroBUZZ (edited 12-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||Jncomutt||12-14-2001||05:32 PM||||Oh yea... And how do these things attach??||||reg||1
Z||000007||AusFiero||12-14-2001||06:02 PM||||You take your door panel off and screw from the back of the door panel into the MDF backing plates in the speaker pods. All screws are hidden.||||reg||1
